   "text": "I read the structure in four parts and wrote the SMILES in that order. Several stereocentres were hard to read and are best guesses, listed at the end.\n\n**Sugar end.** A tetrahydropyran ring has three OH groups, a 2-phosphonoethyl group on one side and a 3-carbon chain on the other. That chain ends in an oxime ether, O\u2013N=C(CH3), carrying a CH2CH2C(=O)NH linker (levulinic-type).\n\n**Lysine linker.**\n- Lys1 is acylated at its \u03b1-nitrogen by levulinic acid, CH3C(=O)CH2CH2C(=O)\u2013.\n- Its \u03b5-NH carries the oxime-linked acyl chain.\n- Its \u03b1-carboxyl is amidated to the \u03b5-NH of Lys2.\n- Lys2 ends as a primary amide, C(N)=O, and its \u03b1-NH is acylated by Gly.\n\n**Macrocycle.** Starting at Cys and following the ring, the residues are:\n- Cys, whose side chain forms a thioether through CH2\u2013S\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013 to the Phe nitrogen\n- Phe, Val, Pro, Thr, Thr\n- Bip (biphenylalanine), N-Me-Ala, Bip, N-Me-Ala\n- Glu, Ala, Pro, which closes back onto the Cys nitrogen\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I worked out the sugar-ring centres from the wedges and hashes, and the lysines, Cys, Val and the N-Me-Alas from their wedges. The rest I assumed.\n- The Phe, Bip and Glu centres are assumed L, with the benzyl and side-chain bonds read as hashed.\n- Both Thr residues are assumed L.\n- The Ala centre next to Glu is assumed L.\n- The lower Pro (next to Thr) is assumed L.\n- The upper Pro (next to Ala) is read as D from its bold wedge.\n\nI could not read the Pro ring bonds or the Ala methyl cleanly in the image, so those assignments are the least certain.\n\nSMILES: OP(=O)(O)CC[C@H]9O[C@@H](CCCON=C(C)CCC(=O)NCCCC[C@H](NC(=O)CCC(C)=O)C(=O)NCCCC[C@H](NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H]%10CSCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(cc1)-c1ccccc1)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(cc1)-c1ccccc1)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N1CCC[C@@H]1C(=O)N%